*> An EXTERNAL file is shared: WRITER opens and closes it, and READER
*> reads it without an OPEN of its own. Neither is reported.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. WRITER.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT SHARED-FILE ASSIGN TO "SHARED".
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD  SHARED-FILE IS EXTERNAL.
01  SHARED-REC          PIC X(20).
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    OPEN OUTPUT SHARED-FILE
    WRITE SHARED-REC FROM "FIRST"
    CALL "READER"
    CLOSE SHARED-FILE
    STOP RUN.
END PROGRAM WRITER.

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. READER.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT SHARED-FILE ASSIGN TO "SHARED".
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD  SHARED-FILE IS EXTERNAL.
01  SHARED-REC          PIC X(20).
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    WRITE SHARED-REC FROM "SECOND"
    GOBACK.
END PROGRAM READER.
